      "text": "1. The sum of the lengths of the two adjacent sides of a square is 40 meters. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ (4x-15) + (20-3x) = 40 \\]\n\n2. Simplify the equation:\n\\[ 4x - 15 + 20 - 3x = 40 \\]\n\\[ x + 5 = 40 \\]\n\n3. Solve for $x$:\n\\[ x = 40 - 5 \\]\n\\[ x = 35 \\]\n\n4. Now that we have the value of $x$, we can find the length of an edge of the square:\n\\[ 4x - 15 = 4(35) - 15 = 140 - 15 = 125 \\]\n\n5. The area of the square is the square of the length of one of its edges:\n\\[ 125^2 = 15625 \\]\n\n6. Therefore, the area of the square is:\n\\[ \\boxed{15625} \\] square meters.",
